Five edits in /srv/patente/webapp/src/main.ts, all in existing structures:

1) The union type (main.ts:20) — currently:
   `type Screen = "home" | "run" | "results" | "profile" | "stats" | "settings";`
   becomes:
   `type Screen = "home" | "run" | "results" | "profile" | "stats" | "vocab" | "settings";`

2) A slot in `state` (main.ts:41-51), mirroring `stats`/`profile`:
```ts
const state: {
  me: Me | null;
  screen: Screen;
  run: Run | null;
  results: SessionResults | null;
  stats: Stats | null;
  profile: Profile | null;
  vocab: Vocabulary | null;          // <- added, from ./types
  resumable: Session | null;
} = { me: null, screen: "home", run: null, results: null, stats: null, profile: null,
      vocab: null, resumable: null };
```

3) One case in render()'s switch (main.ts:1220-1227) — `default:` must stay homeScreen():
```ts
  switch (state.screen) {
    case "run": screen = runScreen(); break;
    case "results": screen = resultsScreen(); break;
    case "profile": screen = profileScreen(); break;
    case "stats": screen = statsScreen(); break;
    case "vocab": screen = vocabScreen(); break;      // <- added
    case "settings": screen = settingsScreen(); break;
    default: screen = homeScreen();
  }
```

4) A tab, so it is reachable (main.ts:1185-1199). `icons.cap` already exists (webapp/src/icons.ts:45); `.tabs` is `display:flex` with `.tab { flex: 1 }` (style.css:378-390), so a fifth tab needs no CSS change:
```ts
  add("home", t("home"), icons.home(23));
  add("profile", t("profile"), icons.person(23));
  add("stats", t("stats"), icons.chart(23));
  add("vocab", t("vocab"), icons.cap(23));            // <- added; t("vocab") exists already
  add("settings", t("settings"), icons.gear(23));
```

5) The screen function + loader, copied from statsScreen (main.ts:902-908) and loadStats (:1029-1036):
```ts
function vocabScreen(): HTMLElement {
  const wrap = el("section", "screen");
  if (!state.vocab) {
    wrap.append(el("div", "spinner"));
    void loadVocab();
    return wrap;
  }
  wrap.append(el("h1", "h1", t("vocab")));
  if (state.vocab.vocabulary_state === "locked") {
    wrap.append(premiumBlock());        // gold = Premium, and nothing else
    return wrap;
  }
  if (state.vocab.vocabulary_state !== "shown" || !state.vocab.terms.length) {
    wrap.append(el("p", "caption", t("vocab_empty")));
    return wrap;
  }
  for (const term of state.vocab.terms) { /* el() + textContent only, never innerHTML */ }
  return wrap;
}

async function loadVocab(): Promise<void> {
  try {
    state.vocab = await api.vocabulary();
    render();
  } catch (err) {
    reportError(err);
  }
}
```

`backTarget()` (main.ts:1201-1210) needs NO change — it is deliberately only for "run" and "results"; a tab-bar screen has no back arrow. And the tab bar (and therefore this screen) stays suppressed during a sitting by the existing guard at :1238-1240.
